      "cooked": "<p>\"When a villain card would enter play, you may discard it instead and destroy this card.\"</p><p>Although I doubt it was the intention, this seems to actually cause an Instant Kill for Miss Information when she flips?</p><p>My thoughts - it has been stated repeatedly that Miss Information is <em>not</em> a target until she flips to Revealed Saboteur, at which point she is treating <em>like any other target that is entering game play</em>...&nbsp; Some might argue that she is a Character Card, rather than simply a Villain Card.&nbsp; However, in previous cases, anytime a hero ability&nbsp;could be used to destroy a card, and they wanted it restricted from hitting Character Cards, it would specifically state something to effect of \"select any card, other than a character card\".&nbsp; Buffer Overflow does not say this... so could she, theoretically, wipe out Miss Information on her flip?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
