      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/bbce88/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-11T17:58:49.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Here's the wording of the original ruling on Miss Information to help:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Christopher\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/48/1851_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Christopher:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The card is not re-entering play. However, the Target aspect of it is. So, no, those cards are not re-entering play and do not need to be reordered or reactivated.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The ruling can be found at <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/25240#comment-25240.&amp;nbsp\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://greaterthangames.com/comment/25240#comment-25240.&amp;nbsp</a>; As Ronway said, the target aspect of Miss Information is entering play, but the card is not—which means Miss Information is not entering play as a villain card, so Buffer Overflow should not trigger.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:22:20.808Z",
